<title>UK: Scottish Hydro sees 45 mln stg one-off hit.</title>
<headline>Scottish Hydro sees 45 mln stg one-off hit.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electricity generator Scottish Hydro-Electric plc expects to pay 45 million stg as its share of a one-off tax on excess profits of privatised utilities to raise 5.2 billion stg announced by the government on Wednesday, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;Scottish Hydro is looking at around 45 million stg,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Chancellor of the Exchequer Gordon Brown earlier told parliament that he would raise 5.2 billion stg through a levy on the excess profits of privatised utilities.</p>
<p>Industry sources said, meanwhile, that nuclear generator British Energy might not have any tax to pay as its flotation value would be above the profits figure used to calculate liability.</p>
<p>Brown said the tax would be based on the difference between flotation values and a formula for net profits for four years after sell-off.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
